    <!--
  The footer earns its place: it is the main defence against a transactional email being
  marked as junk. One captain's address already carries a spam-complaint flag in Mailjet,
  which suppresses delivery to them permanently and leaves no bounce behind to diagnose.
  These emails do go to people who asked for them, but the old ones looked like marketing
  (a SendGrid template complete with hotlinked social icons) and never said why they had
  arrived or who to ask. Saying that plainly is what makes "junk" the wrong button.

  `whyReceiving` is per-email, because the audiences are genuinely different: a captain
  confirming a result, a club secretary receiving a message from the public, and a player
  on the league mailing list should not all be told the same thing. Templates that do not
  set it get the captain wording, which is the common case.
-->
      
